<title>JAPAN: Nippon Steel sets terms on floating rate notes.</title>
<headline>Nippon Steel sets terms on floating rate notes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>BORROWER - Nippon Steel Corp</p>
<p>LEAD MGR - Paribas</p>
<p>FISCAL AGENT - Industrial Bank of Japan</p>
<p>TYPE  floating rate note</p>
<p> ISSUE NO   28	  AMT   10 bln yen</p>
<p>COUPON  coupon will be 2.75 percent minus six months yen LIBOR</p>
<p>in the initial year and be raised every year to 5.15 percent</p>
<p>minus six months yen LIBOR in the seventh year.</p>
<p> ISS PRICE  100 yen   MATURITY 17.Mar.04</p>
<p> LAST MOODY&quot;S	   PAY DATE 17.Mar.    INT PAY 17th Mar/Sep</p>
<p> LAST NIS AA+	   SIGN DATE	     SUB DATE 18.Feb</p>
</text>
